    "q-105681": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105681",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14220023/assets/5a9564ba5a69f4bafa8ff85275ee009b133101aa36c682dd3e50efc949c76d92.png)\n\nConsider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=-4+5y-{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above. What integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+5y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-5y+4 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=1,\\,4.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=1$ to $y=4.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}yf(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}y(-4+5y-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-105681-a",
