    "q-11403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q11403",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=y-2{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis. What integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y(1-2y) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=0$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}yf(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1/2}y(y-2{y}^{2})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
