    "q-105733": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105733",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=\\sqrt{-6+5y-{y}^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis. What integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-6+5y-{y}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ -6+5y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ -({y}^{2}-5y+6) & =0 \\\\ -(y-2)(y-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=2$ and $y=3.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=2$ to $y=3.$\n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}yf(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{3}y\\sqrt{-6+5y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
